{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109362","id":2724896720,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6iap_Q","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109362","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109362.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109362.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109362","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109362/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109362/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109362/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/04408f5b502e0378f1550b40ceb464a00cf29a5d","number":109362,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add support for SDL's audio driver","user":{"login":"kus04e4ek","id":118438257,"node_id":"U_kgDOBw85cQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118438257?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kus04e4ek","html_url":"https://github.com/kus04e4ek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kus04e4ek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kus04e4ek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kus04e4ek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kus04e4ek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kus04e4ek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kus04e4ek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kus04e4ek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kus04e4ek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kus04e4ek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Addresses: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12908\r\nFixes: #98500\r\nFixes: #82823\r\nFixes: #30313\r\n\r\nKeeping it as a draft until I'll finish the TODO list.\r\n\r\nThis PR doesn't bring support for the Web platform as the SDL web audio driver functions the same way as Godot's web audio driver pre-#91382, so it'll most likely break web's audio again.\r\n\r\nTODO:\r\n- [x] Refactor the code, it's not yet ready for review;\r\n- [x] Solve potential deadlocks;\r\n- [ ] Check all of the platforms;\r\n- [ ] Check other GitHub issues to see if this PR solves them.\r\n\r\nAfter merge ([`sdl_audio_extra`](https://github.com/kus04e4ek/godot/tree/sdl_audio_extra) branch contains every change marked off in this section):\r\n- [x] Support changing the SDL backend via the `audio/driver/driver` setting ([here](https://github.com/kus04e4ek/godot/commit/116f3635ed4c32da3807c369ba994670be375d35));\r\n- [x] Report the currently used SDL backend when calling `AudioDriverSDL::get_name()` ([here](https://github.com/kus04e4ek/godot/commit/15e86a788fb8224cd7595107b9cab22b061beaca));\r\n- [x] Support setting the mix rate. SDL does support it, but it [might force devices to use the non-default format which might reduce the number of channels and etc.](https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/blob/b139821903b456021011cbc7ca6abaca6ced3f66/src/audio/SDL_audio.c#L1769) Requires SDL source code modifications, but again wanted to keep the PR minimal ([here](https://github.com/kus04e4ek/godot/commit/77b7e4bc24d92542d46db74ebb3b683cc4eaeabb));\r\n- [ ] Support getting/setting the latency. SDL doesn't provide the support for that and it requires modifications to the SDL source code, it is possible, but I wanted to keep this PR pretty minimal (getting the latency is implemented [here](https://github.com/kus04e4ek/godot/commit/a14002d7270562df33face6ec850ee5f623250ba));\r\n- [ ] Support Android and iOS/visionOS (Depending on the merge order, either this PR or #109645 should be modified, I'll gladly help with porting to these platforms either way);\r\n- [ ] Add `sdl_audio` and `sdl_joypad` build options instead of the one `sdl` option. Not really sure how to tackle it and I don't think it's necessary for this PR;\r\n- [ ] Expose the float buffer for input and output to make SDL type conversion more fast. More about it [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12908#issuecomment-3145618660);\r\n- [ ] Delete `AudioDevice` implementations that are no longer required. Want to make this after making `AudioDriverSDL` feature-complete (latency and mix rate support) as some projects might depend on these features;\r\n- [ ] Evaluate support for the backends not currently supported by Godot.\r\n\r\nSome of these `After merge` goals or all of them can be changed to be included in this PR (especially the ones making the driver feature-complete), curious what y'all think.\r\n\r\nTo check this PR I used slightly modified versions of the demo projects: [demos.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22583269/demos.zip), the driver is set to be SDL and the initialized driver is printed to the console at start, but the `device_changer` demo also has a new button `Update devices`, it just updates the list of available devices and if the device currently used got disconnected, the chosen device in the list will change to the new current device","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471795,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE3OTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:thirdparty","name":"topic:thirdparty","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":572781997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1NzI3ODE5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:audio","name":"topic:audio","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archive